# Build context for the root `Containerfile` (the acme-proxy image, used by the
# e2e lab and as the deployment image).
#
# An allowlist, not a blocklist. The blocklist this replaced named nine paths and
# was wrong in both directions: it let `doc/` (12 MB), `CHANGELOG.md`, `CLAUDE.md`,
# `config.toml.example` and `rfc/` into the context, so editing prose invalidated
# `COPY . .` and forced a full rebuild of the crate; and `*.key`/`ca.pem` match
# only at the root, so `data/ca.key`, `data/ca.pem` and `data/sqlite.db` were
# copied into a build layer. A blocklist has to be extended for every directory
# the repository grows; this does not.
#
# What `cargo build` actually reads:
#   Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock  — the workspace manifest and the pinned graph
#                              (`--locked`)
#   src/                     — the binary and its command tree
#   crates/                  — every library crate of the workspace, including
#                              the assets `include_str!`ed from them
#                              (crates/*/src/webadmin/static/, the `/ui` and
#                              notification templates) and
#                              crates/store/migrations/, which `sqlx::migrate!()`
#                              embeds
#
# `tests/` is deliberately absent: the only thing outside the sources it is
# reached for is `tests/fixtures/rsa_test_key.pk8`, `include_bytes!`d from a
# `#[cfg(test)]` module in the core crate, which a non-test build never compiles.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src/
!crates/
